# IC / controller models — do not reinvent

**WE WILL NOT REINVENT IC OR CONTROLLER BEHAVIOURS.** Fetch an already vendor-provided (or other known reliable) model — same instinct as SPICE `.lib` parts under `public/spice/models/`.

## Do

- Prefer an **existing IC-level** behavioral model from open/MIT engines or license-clear simulator IC sources; document provenance
- Vendor under e.g. `src/avr/vendor/<name>/` + thin facade in `src/avr/<ic>.ts`
- Own **module packaging** ourselves: SVG, pins, bus glue, overlay

## Do not

- Hand-roll controller firmware as the primary path when a working model exists
- Adopt whole-product simulator UI — take the **IC**, not the gadget chrome
- Copy proprietary Proteus/TinkerCAD code (observe only)
- Put bare shared controller ICs in the palette unless you explicitly want that

## When adding a smart module

1. Vendor IC model first
2. Wrap `src/avr/<ic>.ts`
3. Then PartModule (artwork + pins + evaluate/overlay)

See also `no-invent-simulation.mdc` (V/I from AVR/SPICE) and `new-components.mdc` (registry / SVG checklist).
